quirements (product-manager), Design (architect), UX (designer), Docs (documentation-planner) and Implementation (engineer), and a value in `config.yaml` overrides that; a triage role with none may write only its own role file. There are no per-role config files: `ard init` writes a role's starting overrides into `config.yaml` for the roles it ships. Once a second repo adopts ard, role directories can move to a shared roles repo pinned by ref, like a sidecar; a repo's own directory of the same name wins. `after` names triage roles, with no self-reference and no cycles.\n \n-**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n+**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `scanners/trufflehog`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\n \n **Where `ard serve` reads config (decided, #87).** After each fetch into its own clone (`~/.ard/repos/<owner>/<repo>.git`, see Local-executor details) `ard serve` resolves `origin/main` to a SHA and reads `config.yaml` and the role directories from that commit, not from the working tree. It exports them into a snapshot at `~/.ard/config/<owner>/<repo>/<sha>/`, kept 24 hours after a newer SHA replaces it, because roles run from a host path: a role directory, its `Dockerfile` and the scan worktree must all describe the one commit the tick's jobs use. Editing the host's working tree therefore changes nothing on a running controller, with one exception: a local `paused: true` is honoured (see the kill switch), and only that key is read locally. A merged change applies on the next tick without a pull. Symlinks and submodules under the role directories are rejected, and a config that cannot be fetched or does not validate counts as paused. If `origin/main` cannot be loaded at startup, `ard serve` starts paused instead of exiting, posts the load error to the status issue once per distinct error, and retries every tick; no loop runs until a config has loaded. `ard config check` validates the working tree, for authoring; `ard config check --ref <ref>` validates a commit of the local checkout (for example `--ref origin/main` after `git fetch`) without fetching.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/body.go b/internal/initcmd/body.go\nindex b9fea42..6a5ccd0 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/body.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/body.go\n@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ func initBody(ops []op, res *config.Resolved) string {\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Before you merge\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Nothing takes effect until this is merged: ard serve reads its configuration from origin/main.\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"- Merge with **Squash and merge** (recommended); **Create a merge commit** is also safe. Never fast-forward this branch into main from the command line: the bot-commit check reads main's first-parent history and would fail on the bot's commit.\\n\")\n+\tb.WriteString(\"- `scanners/trufflehog` is included. It files leaked-credential issues for a human (never for an agent) and needs a TruffleHog binary (AGPL-3.0; it is installed by the role's Dockerfile or taken from the host, and is not in the ard image). To opt out, delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` and its `scanners/trufflehog` line under `overrides:` in `.ard/config.yaml` before merging.\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"\\n## Follow-up the App cannot do\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"ard's GitHub App has no permission to write `.github/`, so do this by hand:\\n\\n\")\n \tb.WriteString(\"1. Copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` from the ard repository into this repository.\\n\")\ndiff --git a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\nindex 09ee735..dccb5e8 100644\n--- a/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n+++ b/internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go\n@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ func snapshot(t *testing.T, dir string) map[string]string {\n \treturn m\n }\n \n-var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n+var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n \n func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n \th := newHarness(t)\n@@ -198,7 +198,7 @@ func TestInitOpensPR(t *testing.T) {\n \tif pr.HeadRef != \"ard-init\" || pr.BaseRef != \"main\" || pr.Draft {\n \t\tt.Errorf(\"pr = %+v\", pr)\n \t}\n-\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"delete `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/`\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n \t\tif !strings.Contains(pr.Body, s) {\n \t\t\tt.Errorf(\"PR body lacks %q:\\n%s\", s, pr.Body)\n \t\t}\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/config.yaml b/internal/roles/config.yaml\nindex a72acd4..fc4954c 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/config.yaml\n+++ b/internal/roles/config.yaml\n@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@ overrides:\n   scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n   scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n+  # Leaked credentials go straight to a human: route: needs-human files without\n+  # ard:pending, so no agent triages them.\n+  scanners/trufflehog: { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\n   triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n   triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n   # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/roles.go b/internal/roles/roles.go\nindex 7f2526f..272d965 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/roles.go\n+++ b/internal/roles/roles.go\n@@ -7,11 +7,11 @@ package roles\n import \"embed\"\n \n // FS is the starter .ard/ tree `ard init` proposes: config.yaml plus the role\n-// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n+// directories (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/trufflehog, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review and reviewers/security-review); paths are relative to .ard/.\n //\n // scanners/missing-tests is left out until its scan driver exists; re-add it when wiring it in.\n //\n-//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes triage workers\n+//go:embed config.yaml reviewers scanners/cve scanners/docs scanners/error-codes scanners/trufflehog triage workers\n var FS embed.FS\n \n // ExecutableNames lists base names that must be written 0755.\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/roles_test.go b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\nindex 84698ba..747cad1 100644\n--- a/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n+++ b/internal/roles/roles_test.go\n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatal(err)\n \t}\n \tsort.Strings(got)\n-\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n+\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\", \"scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n \tif strings.Join(got, \",\") != strings.Join(want, \",\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"embedded files = %v, want %v\", got, want)\n \t}\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ func TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n // embed.FS reports 0444 for everything, so the exec bit must be checked on disk\n // to catch a mode lost in git.\n func TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk(t *testing.T) {\n-\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\"} {\n+\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"scanners/trufflehog/scan\"} {\n \t\tfi, err := os.Stat(p)\n \t\tif err != nil {\n \t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n@@ -168,3 +168,29 @@ func starterFS(t *testing.T, chmod bool) fstest.MapFS {\n \t}\n \treturn m\n }\n+\n+func TestEmbeddedTrufflehogRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n+\tres, err := config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, true), \"/repo\")\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFS: %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, r := range res.Roles {\n+\t\tif r.Kind != config.KindScanner || r.Name != \"trufflehog\" {\n+\t\t\tcontinue\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.ScanPath != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/scan\" || !r.Autoclose || r.Every != 24*time.Hour || r.GroupSize != 1 || r.MaxOpen != 5 || r.Timeout != 30*time.Minute {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected role: %+v\", r)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.Route != config.RouteNeedsHuman {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Route = %v, want needs-human\", r.Route)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif r.Dockerfile != \".ard/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\" {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Dockerfile = %q\", r.Dockerfile)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !slices.Equal(r.Extra, []string{\"exclude-paths\", \"findings.jq\"}) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Extra = %v, want [exclude-paths findings.jq]\", r.Extra)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tt.Fatal(\"no scanner role trufflehog\")\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3d54fc7\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\n@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@\n+# Pinned tool image for the trufflehog scanner. Versions verified 2026-11-23:\n+#   trufflehog 3.100.0 (released 2026-11-19), jq 1.8.2.\n+# The trufflehog tarball checksums come from trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt,\n+# whose signature was verified on 2026-11-23 with cosign v3.1.4 (\"Verified OK\"):\n+#   cosign verify-blob trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt \\\n+#     --certificate trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.pem \\\n+#     --signature trufflehog_3.100.0_checksums.txt.sig \\\n+#     --certificate-identity-regexp 'https://github\\.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/' \\\n+#     --certificate-oidc-issuer https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\n+# jq's checksums are the ones in scanners/cve/Dockerfile.\n+# The base is the same golang:1.27.4-trixie index digest as cve and the ard\n+# image (root Dockerfile), so the layers are shared.\n+#\n+# LICENCE: trufflehog is AGPL-3.0. It is downloaded into this role's image only;\n+# the binary is NOT in the published ard image.\n+#\n+# The image does NOT copy `scan` or `findings.jq`: the executor mounts this role\n+# directory read-only, so the mounted script is always the one that runs.\n+# Run:  docker run --rm -v \"$PWD\":/repo:ro -v <role dir>:/role:ro -w /repo IMAGE /role/scan\n+\n+ARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n+\n+FROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\n+ARG TARGETARCH\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=3.100.0\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64=b2d85eba59865e98f45c9fc9f77d2c6d62df529fdd5755af121304ea5a7cecbb\n+ARG TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64=aa61657049229ae523e8455fcbba87dff57b0a2ba6bdb391a38cf75e6d4016dd\n+ARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\n+ARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\n+ARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\n+RUN set -eu; \\\n+    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n+      amd64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_AMD64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n+      arm64) th_sha=\"${TRUFFLEHOG_SHA256_ARM64}\"; jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n+      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n+    esac; \\\n+    mkdir /out; \\\n+    curl -fsSL -o /tmp/th.tgz \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_${TARGETARCH}.tar.gz\"; \\\n+    echo \"${th_sha}  /tmp/th.tgz\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n+    tar -xzf /tmp/th.tgz -C /out trufflehog; \\\n+    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n+    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n+    chmod 0755 /out/trufflehog /out/jq\n+\n+FROM ${GO_IMAGE}\n+COPY --from=tools /out/trufflehog /usr/local/bin/trufflehog\n+COPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n+# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs; keep the temp dir in /var/tmp.\n+ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..b83ab0b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+# trufflehog path regexes (Go RE2), one per line, matched against repo-relative\n+# paths. Human-owned: change it in a reviewed PR. scan drops # lines and blanks.\n+# .ard/<n>/logs/ were secret-scanned at close-out (model signature blobs are noise).\n+^\\.ard/[0-9]+/logs/\n+^vendor/\n+^node_modules/\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..23ef8a6\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/findings.jq\n@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@\n+# project: trufflehog --json result lines in; one \"<base64 secret>\\t<json>\" line out\n+#          per result. The json holds only d (DetectorName), f (file), l (line).\n+#          Errors carry fixed text only (scan drops this stage's stderr anyway).\n+# merge:   \"<h16>\\t<json>\" lines in (-n -R, inputs); findings out.\n+def die(m): error(\"trufflehog: \" + m);\n+\n+def project:\n+  if type != \"object\" then die(\"result is not an object\") else . end\n+  | (.SourceMetadata.Data.Filesystem // die(\"result has no filesystem location\")) as $fs\n+  | (if (.Raw | type) == \"string\" and .Raw != \"\" then .Raw\n+     elif (.RawV2 | type) == \"string\" and .RawV2 != \"\" then .RawV2\n+     else die(\"result has no Raw or RawV2 value\") end) as $secret\n+  | (.DetectorName | if type == \"string\" and test(\"^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,64}$\") then . else die(\"bad detector name\") end) as $d\n+  | ($fs.file | if type == \"string\" then ltrimstr(\"./\") else die(\"result file is not a string\") end) as $f\n+  | if $f == \"\" or ($f | startswith(\"/\")) or ($f | split(\"/\") | any(. == \"..\" or . == \".\" or . == \"\"))\n+       or ($f | explode | any(. < 32 or . == 127))\n+    then die(\"result file is not a clean repo-relative path\") else . end\n+  | ($fs.line // 0 | if type == \"number\" and . >= 0 then floor else die(\"bad line\") end) as $l\n+  | \"\\($secret | @base64)\\t\\({d: $d, f: $f, l: $l} | tojson)\";\n+\n+# A code span whose fence is longer than any backtick run in the text.\n+def code: ([match(\"`+\"; \"g\").length] | max // 0) as $n | (\"`\" * ($n + 1)) as $fence\n+  | if $n > 0 then \"\\($fence) \\(.) \\($fence)\" else \"\\($fence)\\(.)\\($fence)\" end;\n+\n+def merge($allow):\n+  [inputs | select(length > 0) | split(\"\\t\")\n+   | if length != 2 or (.[0] | test(\"^[0-9a-f]{16}$\") | not) then die(\"bad hashed line\") else . end\n+   | {h: .[0]} + (.[1] | fromjson)]\n+  | map(select((\"trufflehog:\" + .h) as $fp | $allow | index($fp) | not))\n+  | group_by(.h)\n+  | map((\"trufflehog:\" + .[0].h) as $fp\n+      | (map(.d) | unique) as $dets\n+      | (map({f, l}) | unique_by([.f, .l]) | sort_by(.f, .l)) as $locs\n+      | ($locs | map(.f) | unique) as $files\n+      | {fingerprint: $fp,\n+         title: (\"Possible \\($dets[0]) credential in \\($files[0])\" | .[0:200]),\n+         severity: \"high\", group: \"\", files: $files[0:1000],\n+         body: ([\n+           \"trufflehog matched a value that looks like a credential (detector: \\($dets | map(code) | join(\", \"))). ard did not verify it and never stores or prints the value.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"**Treat it as leaked.** Revoke or rotate it at the provider first. Deleting the line does not revoke it: the value stays in git history, and on a public repository it is already public.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"**Do not add `ard:pending` to this issue before the credential is rotated.** Triage and worker agents would read the file that holds it.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"What to do: 1. Rotate or revoke the credential at the provider. 2. Remove the value from HEAD in a PR. The issue closes itself on the next run (within 24 hours) once the value is gone from HEAD; that means gone from HEAD, not rotated. 3. Do not close this issue as completed while the value is still at HEAD: the next run refiles it. 4. For a false positive or a test fixture, add the fingerprint to `allow` or the path to `exclude-paths` (a reviewed PR), or close as not planned (it refiles after 90 days). 5. At 5 open issues the scanner does not run, so close fixed ones by hand once the value is gone. 6. Git history is not scanned or rewritten; rotation is what makes that safe.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Not a secret? A maintainer adds the fingerprint below to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/allow`, or a path pattern to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/exclude-paths`, in a reviewed PR. Inline `trufflehog:ignore` comments are not honoured.\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Fingerprint: `\\($fp)`\",\n+           \"\",\n+           \"Locations at the scanned commit (\\($locs | length)):\"]\n+           + ($locs[0:50] | map(\"- \\(.f | code)\" + (if .l > 0 then \" line \\(.l)\" else \"\" end)))\n+           + (if ($locs | length) > 50 then [\"- and \\(($locs | length) - 50) more\"] else [] end)\n+           + (if ($files | length) > 1000 then [\"\", \"Only the first 1,000 of \\($files | length) files are listed.\"] else [] end)\n+           | join(\"\\n\"))})\n+  | sort_by(.fingerprint) | .[];\n+\n+if $stage == \"project\" then project\n+elif $stage == \"merge\" then merge($allow | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"#.*$\"; \"\") | gsub(\"^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$\"; \"\")) | map(select(. != \"\")))\n+else die(\"unknown stage\") end\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan\nnew file mode 100755\nindex 0000000..2b35737\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/scan\n@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+#!/bin/sh\n+# trufflehog scanner: files leaked-credential findings for a human.\n+#\n+# Contract: run from the repository root (cwd) on the current commit. Sibling\n+# files (findings.jq, exclude-paths, allow) are found from this script's own\n+# path. Writes only to a temp dir. Needs no token. stdout (JSON lines, one\n+# finding each) is printed only at the very end. Exit 0 = ok, 1 = failed\n+# (nothing on stdout), 2 = a required tool is missing.\n+#\n+# Owner rules: no verification (--no-verification: no credential is ever sent\n+# to a provider); HEAD only (filesystem scan, no history); only DetectorName,\n+# the file, the line and a hash of the secret leave the project stage: Raw,\n+# RawV2, Redacted, SecretParts, ExtraData, StructuredData and the rest never\n+# leave this script. The secret exists only in pipes: never in a file, argv,\n+# stdout or stderr. --no-ignore-tag: inline trufflehog:ignore is not honoured.\n+#\n+# Human-owned files next to this script: exclude-paths (regexes) and allow\n+# (one trufflehog:<16 hex> fingerprint per line, # comments). A bad allow\n+# entry fails the run. .git is always excluded.\n+#\n+# Never pass --since-commit, --max-depth, --detector-timeout, --archive-timeout,\n+# --filter-unverified, --filter-entropy or --results: a partial or\n+# load-dependent result would make the pipeline autoclose live findings.\n+# Never use set -x: it would print the secret.\n+set -eu\n+dir=$(CDPATH= cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\n+die() { echo \"trufflehog: $*\" >&2; exit 1; }\n+need() { command -v \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \"trufflehog: $1 not found\" >&2; exit 2; }; }\n+need trufflehog\n+need jq\n+if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sha() { sha256sum; }\n+elif command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sha() { shasum -a 256; }\n+else echo \"trufflehog: sha256sum not found\" >&2; exit 2; fi\n+\n+tmp=$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/ard-trufflehog.XXXXXX\")\n+trap 'rm -rf \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n+trap 'exit 130' INT\n+trap 'exit 143' TERM\n+\n+echo \"trufflehog: $(trufflehog --version 2>&1 | head -n 1 || true)\" >&2\n+\n+# Exclusions: .git always, then the human-owned file without comments or blanks.\n+printf '%s\\n' '^\\.git(/|$)' > \"$tmp/exclude\"\n+if [ -e \"$dir/exclude-paths\" ]; then\n+  grep -v -e '^[[:space:]]*#' -e '^[[:space:]]*$' \"$dir/exclude-paths\" >> \"$tmp/exclude\" || true\n+fi\n+allow=$tmp/allow.txt\n+: > \"$allow\"\n+[ ! -e \"$dir/allow\" ] || cat \"$dir/allow\" > \"$allow\"\n+jq -n -R --rawfile allow \"$allow\" '$allow | split(\"\\n\") | map(sub(\"#.*$\"; \"\") | gsub(\"^\\\\s+|\\\\s+$\"; \"\"))\n+  | map(select(. != \"\")) | if any(test(\"^trufflehog:[0-9a-f]{16}$\") | not) then error(\"bad\") else empty end' 2>/dev/null \\\n+  || die \"allow: every entry must be trufflehog:<16 hex digits> (comments start with #)\"\n+\n+tab=$(printf '\\t')\n+# The secret exists only in these pipes: never in a file, argv, stdout or stderr.\n+# Each stage records its own status (no pipefail in POSIX sh); \"|| rc=$?\" keeps\n+# set -e from skipping the echo.\n+{\n+  rc=0\n+  trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification \\\n+    --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2 -x \"$tmp/exclude\" \\\n+    2>\"$tmp/th.err\" || rc=$?\n+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/th.rc\"\n+} | {\n+  rc=0\n+  # stderr dropped: a jq type error can quote the input, which holds the secret.\n+  jq -r --arg stage project --arg allow \"\" -f \"$dir/findings.jq\" 2>/dev/null || rc=$?\n+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/project.rc\"\n+} | {\n+  rc=0\n+  while IFS=$tab read -r pre rest; do\n+    h=$(printf 'ard-trufflehog-v1\\000%s' \"$pre\" | sha | cut -c1-16) || { rc=1; break; }\n+    case $h in *[!0-9a-f]*|'') rc=1; break ;; esac\n+    [ ${#h} -eq 16 ] || { rc=1; break; }\n+    printf '%s\\t%s\\n' \"$h\" \"$rest\"\n+  done\n+  echo \"$rc\" > \"$tmp/hash.rc\"\n+} > \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\"\n+\n+rcof() { [ -s \"$tmp/$1.rc\" ] && cat \"$tmp/$1.rc\" || echo missing; }\n+th=$(rcof th)\n+if [ \"$th\" != 0 ]; then\n+  jq -r 'select(.level == \"error\") | \"trufflehog: \\(.msg // \"\") \\((.error // \"\") | tostring | .[0:200])\"' \\\n+    \"$tmp/th.err\" 2>/dev/null | head -n 5 >&2 || true\n+  die \"trufflehog failed (exit status $th)\"\n+fi\n+[ \"$(rcof project)\" = 0 ] || die \"cannot parse trufflehog results\"\n+[ \"$(rcof hash)\" = 0 ] || die \"cannot hash a result\"\n+\n+summary=$(jq -c 'select(.msg == \"finished scanning\") | [.chunks, .verified_secrets, .unverified_secrets]' \\\n+  \"$tmp/th.err\" 2>/dev/null | tail -n 1) || die \"cannot read trufflehog's log\"\n+case $summary in\n+  \\[[0-9]*,[0-9]*,[0-9]*\\]) ;;\n+  *) die \"no \\\"finished scanning\\\" summary from trufflehog\" ;;\n+esac\n+set -- $(echo \"$summary\" | tr -d '[]' | tr ',' ' ')\n+chunks=$1 want=$(($2 + $3))\n+got=$(wc -l < \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\" | tr -d ' ')\n+echo \"trufflehog: $chunks chunk(s), $got result(s)\" >&2\n+if [ \"$chunks\" -eq 0 ] && [ -n \"$(find . -name .git -prune -o -type f -print | head -n 1)\" ]; then\n+  die \"trufflehog scanned nothing in a non-empty tree (or every file is excluded)\"\n+fi\n+[ \"$got\" -eq \"$want\" ] || die \"result count $got does not match the summary's $want\"\n+\n+jq -n -R -c --arg stage merge --rawfile allow \"$allow\" -f \"$dir/findings.jq\" \"$tmp/hashed.tsv\" \\\n+  > \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" || die \"merge failed\"\n+echo \"trufflehog: $(wc -l < \"$tmp/out.jsonl\" | tr -d ' ') finding(s)\" >&2\n+cat \"$tmp/out.jsonl\"\ndiff --git a/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go b/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..59d6f29\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/roles/trufflehog_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,292 @@\n+package roles\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"bytes\"\n+\t\"encoding/json\"\n+\t\"os\"\n+\t\"os/exec\"\n+\t\"path/filepath\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/scanner\"\n+)\n+\n+// thFake stands in for trufflehog: it records argv and replays stdout, stderr\n+// and the exit code from files named by the environment.\n+const thFake = `#!/bin/sh\n+if [ \"${1:-}\" = --version ]; then echo \"trufflehog 3.100.0\"; exit 0; fi\n+printf '%s\\n' \"$*\" >> \"$TH_ARGV\"\n+[ -z \"${TH_STDOUT:-}\" ] || cat \"$TH_STDOUT\"\n+[ -z \"${TH_STDERR:-}\" ] || cat \"$TH_STDERR\" >&2\n+exit \"${TH_RC:-0}\"\n+`\n+\n+type thResult struct {\n+\tstdout, stderr string\n+\tcode           int\n+\targv           string\n+\ttmp            string\n+}\n+\n+type thLine map[string]any\n+\n+func thResultLine(raw, det, file string, line int) thLine {\n+\treturn thLine{\"DetectorName\": det, \"Raw\": raw, \"RawV2\": \"v2-marker\", \"Redacted\": \"redacted-marker\",\n+\t\t\"SourceMetadata\": map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Filesystem\": map[string]any{\"file\": file, \"line\": line}}}}\n+}\n+\n+func thSummary(chunks, unverified int) string {\n+\tb, _ := json.Marshal(map[string]any{\"level\": \"info\", \"msg\": \"finished scanning\", \"chunks\": chunks, \"verified_secrets\": 0, \"unverified_secrets\": unverified})\n+\treturn string(b)\n+}\n+\n+func thJoin(lines []thLine) string {\n+\tvar sb strings.Builder\n+\tfor _, l := range lines {\n+\t\tb, _ := json.Marshal(l)\n+\t\tsb.Write(b)\n+\t\tsb.WriteByte('\\n')\n+\t}\n+\treturn sb.String()\n+}\n+\n+// thRun runs the shipped scan in a temp repo with a fake trufflehog.\n+func thRun(t *testing.T, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\treturn thRunFull(t, mustAbs(t, \"scanners/trufflehog\"), out, errlog, rc, files, extra)\n+}\n+\n+func thRunWith(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\treturn thRunFull(t, role, out, errlog, rc, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n+}\n+\n+func thRunFull(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int, files map[string]string, extra map[string]string) thResult {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tneedTools(t, \"sh\", \"jq\")\n+\tif _, err := exec.LookPath(\"sha256sum\"); err != nil {\n+\t\tneedTools(t, \"shasum\")\n+\t}\n+\twork := t.TempDir()\n+\trepo := filepath.Join(work, \"repo\")\n+\tbin := filepath.Join(work, \"bin\")\n+\ttmp := filepath.Join(work, \"tmp\")\n+\tfor _, d := range []string{repo, bin, tmp} {\n+\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(d, 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(bin, \"trufflehog\"), []byte(thFake), 0o755); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor name, body := range files {\n+\t\tp := filepath.Join(repo, name)\n+\t\tos.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(p), 0o755)\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(p, []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tfor name, body := range map[string]string{\"stdout\": out, \"stderr\": errlog} {\n+\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(work, name), []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tcmd := exec.Command(\"sh\", filepath.Join(role, \"scan\"))\n+\tcmd.Dir = repo\n+\tcmd.Env = []string{\"PATH=\" + bin + \":\" + os.Getenv(\"PATH\"), \"TMPDIR=\" + tmp, \"TH_ARGV=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"argv\"),\n+\t\t\"TH_STDOUT=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"stdout\"), \"TH_STDERR=\" + filepath.Join(work, \"stderr\"), \"TH_RC=\" + string(rune('0'+rc))}\n+\tfor k, v := range extra {\n+\t\tcmd.Env = append(cmd.Env, k+\"=\"+v)\n+\t}\n+\tvar so, se bytes.Buffer\n+\tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = &so, &se\n+\tcode := 0\n+\tif err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n+\t\tee, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError)\n+\t\tif !ok {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tcode = ee.ExitCode()\n+\t}\n+\targv, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(work, \"argv\"))\n+\treturn thResult{so.String(), se.String(), code, string(argv), tmp}\n+}\n+\n+func thTmpEmpty(t *testing.T, tmp string) {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tif ents, _ := os.ReadDir(tmp); len(ents) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"temp dir not cleaned: %v\", ents)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTrufflehogAggregatesAndFingerprints(t *testing.T) {\n+\tin := thJoin([]thLine{\n+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Zeta\", \"sub/b.txt\", 3),\n+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1),\n+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"./a.txt\", 1),\n+\t\tthResultLine(\"canary-raw-beta\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 2),\n+\t})\n+\tr := thRun(t, in, thSummary(2, 4), 0, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n+\tif r.code != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit %d: %s\", r.code, r.stderr)\n+\t}\n+\tfs, err := scanner.DecodeFindings(strings.NewReader(r.stdout))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tif len(fs) != 2 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"findings = %d, want 2:\\n%s\", len(fs), r.stdout)\n+\t}\n+\tgot := map[string]scanner.Finding{}\n+\tfor _, f := range fs {\n+\t\tgot[f.Fingerprint] = f\n+\t}\n+\talpha, ok := got[\"trufflehog:d4bf4d1967fad7b7\"]\n+\tif !ok || got[\"trufflehog:ce658c895bb3b307\"].Fingerprint == \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"golden fingerprints missing:\\n%s\", r.stdout)\n+\t}\n+\tif alpha.Title != \"Possible Alpha credential in a.txt\" || alpha.Severity != \"high\" || strings.Join(alpha.Files, \",\") != \"a.txt,sub/b.txt\" {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"alpha = %+v\", alpha)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"Do not add `ard:pending`\", \"1. Rotate\", \"6. Git history\"} {\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(alpha.Body, s) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"body lacks %q\", s)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, leak := range []string{\"canary-raw\", \"v2-marker\", \"redacted-marker\"} {\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(r.stdout+r.stderr, leak) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%q leaked\", leak)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tthTmpEmpty(t, r.tmp)\n+\t// deterministic: reversed input gives identical stdout\n+\tlines := strings.Split(strings.TrimSpace(in), \"\\n\")\n+\tfor i, j := 0, len(lines)-1; i < j; i, j = i+1, j-1 {\n+\t\tlines[i], lines[j] = lines[j], lines[i]\n+\t}\n+\tr2 := thRun(t, strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")+\"\\n\", thSummary(2, 4), 0, map[string]string{\"a.txt\": \"x\"}, nil)\n+\tif r2.stdout != r.stdout {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"output depends on input order\")\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTrufflehogFailsClosed(t *testing.T) {\n+\tok := thResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1)\n+\tbad := func(mut func(thLine)) string {\n+\t\tl := thResultLine(\"canary-raw-alpha\", \"Alpha\", \"a.txt\", 1)\n+\t\tmut(l)\n+\t\treturn thJoin([]thLine{l})\n+\t}\n+\tfsData := func(l thLine, file any) {\n+\t\tl[\"SourceMetadata\"] = map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Filesystem\": map[string]any{\"file\": file}}}\n+\t}\n+\tcases := []struct {\n+\t\tname, out, log string\n+\t\trc             int\n+\t\tallow          string\n+\t\twant           string\n+\t}{\n+\t\t{\"exit1\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 1, \"\", \"failed (exit status 1)\"},\n+\t\t{\"exit2\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 2, \"\", \"failed (exit status 2)\"},\n+\t\t{\"no summary\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), \"\", 0, \"\", \"finished scanning\"},\n+\t\t{\"zero chunks\", \"\", thSummary(0, 0), 0, \"\", \"scanned nothing\"},\n+\t\t{\"count mismatch\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 2), 0, \"\", \"does not match\"},\n+\t\t{\"malformed\", \"{not json\\n\", thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"non-object\", \"[1]\\n\", thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"absolute path\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"/etc/x\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"dotdot\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"../x\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"inner dotdot\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"a/../b\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"control char\", bad(func(l thLine) { fsData(l, \"a\\nb\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"git source\", bad(func(l thLine) { l[\"SourceMetadata\"] = map[string]any{\"Data\": map[string]any{\"Git\": map[string]any{}}} }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"no raw\", bad(func(l thLine) { delete(l, \"Raw\"); delete(l, \"RawV2\") }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"bad detector\", bad(func(l thLine) { l[\"DetectorName\"] = \"bad name!\" }), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"\", \"cannot parse\"},\n+\t\t{\"bad allow\", thJoin([]thLine{ok}), thSummary(1, 1), 0, \"nonsense\\n\", \"allow:\"},\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, c := range cases {\n+\t\tt.Run(c.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n+\t\t\tneedTools(t, \"sh\", \"jq\")\n+\t\t\trole := mustAbs(t, \"scanners/trufflehog\")\n+\t\t\tif c.allow != \"\" { // allow lives beside scan: use a copy of the role dir\n+\t\t\t\tcp := t.TempDir()\n+\t\t\t\tfor _, n := range []string{\"scan\", \"findings.jq\", \"exclude-paths\"} {\n+\t\t\t\t\tb, _ := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(role, n))\n+\t\t\t\t\tos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(cp, n), b, 0o755)\n+\t\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\t\tos.WriteFile(filepath.Join(cp, \"allow\"), []byte(c.allow), 0o644)\n+\t\t\t\trole = cp\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tr := thRunRole(t, role, c.out, c.log, c.rc)\n+\t\t\tif r.code == 0 || r.stdout != \"\" {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"exit %d, stdout %q; want failure with empty stdout\", r.code, r.stdout)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(r.stderr, c.want) {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr lacks %q:\\n%s\", c.want, r.stderr)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif strings.Contains(r.stderr, \"canary-raw\") {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"stderr leaks the secret:\\n%s\", r.stderr)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tthTmpEmpty(t, r.tmp)\n+\t\t})\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+// thRunRole is thRun against another role directory (used for allow files).\n+func thRunRole(t *testing.T, role, out, errlog string, rc int) thResult {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\treturn thRunWith(t, role, out, errlog, rc)\n+}\n+\n+func TestTrufflehogArgvAndExcludes(t *testing.T) {\n+\tr := thRun(t, \"\", thSummary(0, 0), 0, nil, nil)\n+\tif r.code != 0 || r.stdout != \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"empty repo: exit %d stdout %q stderr %s\", r.code, r.stdout, r.stderr)\n+\t}\n+\targv := strings.TrimSpace(r.argv)\n+\tif !strings.HasPrefix(argv, \"filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2 -x \") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"argv = %q\", argv)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, f := range []string{\"--since-commit\", \"--max-depth\", \"--detector-timeout\", \"--archive-timeout\", \"--filter-unverified\", \"--filter-entropy\", \"--results\", \"--include-detectors\", \"--exclude-detectors\", \"--json-legacy\"} {\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(argv, f) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"forbidden flag %s in argv\", f)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tthTmpEmpty(t, r.tmp)\n+}\n+\n+func TestTrufflehogMissingTool(t *testing.T) {\n+\tneedTools(t, \"sh\")\n+\tcmd := exec.Command(\"/bin/sh\", filepath.Join(mustAbs(t, \"scanners/trufflehog\"), \"scan\"))\n+\tcmd.Env = []string{\"PATH=\" + t.TempDir()}\n+\tvar so, se bytes.Buffer\n+\tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = &so, &se\n+\terr := cmd.Run()\n+\tee, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError)\n+\tif !ok || ee.ExitCode() != 2 || so.Len() != 0 || !strings.Contains(se.String(), \"trufflehog not found\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err %v stdout %q stderr %q\", err, so.String(), se.String())\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestTrufflehogDockerfilePins(t *testing.T) {\n+\tth, _ := os.ReadFile(\"scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile\")\n+\tcve, _ := os.ReadFile(\"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\")\n+\tpin := func(b []byte) string {\n+\t\tfor _, l := range strings.Split(string(b), \"\\n\") {\n+\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(l, \"ARG GO_IMAGE=\") {\n+\t\t\t\treturn l\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn \"\"\n+\t}\n+\tif pin(th) == \"\" || pin(th) != pin(cve) {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"GO_IMAGE pin differs from cve's\")\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, s := range []string{\"ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\", \"ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=\", \"sha256sum -c\"} {\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(string(th), s) {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"Dockerfile lacks %q\", s)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif strings.Contains(string(th), \"COPY scan\") || strings.Contains(string(th), \"findings.jq /\") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"Dockerfile must not copy scan files\")\n+\t}\n+}\n","numLines":736,"startLine":1,"totalLines":736}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017FQVQtBStrNsr8zRjiEJtQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
